First Author: Adedinsewo
Title: Non-invasive detection of cardiac allograft rejection among heart transplant recipients using an electrocardiogram based deep learning model
Source number: 1 (based on the uploaded PDF filename: 1_Adedinsewo et al. - 2023 ...pdf)  ￼

Very short summary: This study developed and tested a deep-learning 12-lead ECG model (AI-ECG) to detect moderate-to-severe acute cellular rejection (ACR) after heart transplantation. Five key findings were: (1) the retrospective development cohort included 1427 patients and 7590 ECG-biopsy pairs; (2) the held-out test set included 140 patients and 758 ECG-biopsy pairs; (3) the AI-ECG achieved test AUC 0.84 with 95% sensitivity and 99.7% negative predictive value at the chosen threshold; (4) a prospective proof-of-concept cohort of 56 patients and 97 ECG-biopsy pairs showed AUC 0.78 with 100% sensitivity; and (5) the model outperformed standard ECG variables alone, which had AUC 0.579. Figures and tables showed the study flow, model architecture, ROC performance, subgroup performance, and differences in demographic/ECG characteristics by rejection status.  ￼  ￼  ￼

