	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper says it “initially conducted a retrospective cohort study,” then a prospective proof-of-concept study after model development. The model was “a convolutional neural-network model” using the “12-lead ECG signal as input.” The retrospective data were split into training/validation/test sets. Figure 2 describes the architecture, and the paper states the best model was chosen after “a randomized hyperparameter search over optimizer, learning rates, class weights, batch size, and regularization.” The comparator was not a single clinical rule or human reader; the paper compares against standard ECG variables alone, which had inferior AUC 0.579.  ￼  ￼

